Here's my story of what may very well be the stupidest way to die
of all time:  ;)
 
My poor Valkrye was wandering around on level 5 or so when a Nymph 
came along and stole everything except a spare black knife and a food 
ration I was carrying.  I quickly wielded the dagger, but hit the
wrong key and wielded the food ration instead.  Of course, the food
ration was cursed.  But wait!  I can EAT my way out of it...so I ate
the food ration and choked on it and died.  (Note that this was an 
older version that didn't let you 'Stop eating?').
 
On the other side - the best character I ever had that I was trying
desperately to kill:  
 
I was testing the reverse video mode (or something like that) and
was just playing a Valykre (named:  'Death!!') to see how it looked.
The first space he started on had a wand.  No prob!  I'll just zap
myself and die..it was an invisibilty wand.  So I decided to just make
a dash for the stairs and whenever I found them I would go down without
exploring the rest of the level.  In the second room I found a ring of
polymorph and got polymorphed into a Minatour....no matter how hard
I tried, this guy wouldn't die!!!  :)  Eventally I think he died from
a system shock on level 22.  Jeez!
 
And one last note:  the 'very funny' game.  I hadn't had any armor
for the first 10 levels other than the studded leather I started with.
Finally on level 11 I find - yes, there in the corner, a suit of
Crystal Plate mail!  I rush to it and put it on.  Moving to the left,
I of course hit a polymorph trap, burst out of the armor...aaaaaaaaagggg
 
*grin*
 
